---
description: Outbound mail only. No inbox, no IMAP, no caller-supplied letter.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Outbound mail

The app sends mail. It does not receive mail.

Do not open IMAP, port 143, or port 993. Do not read a mailbox, wait for a reply, or copy a message into Sent.

SMTP ports are only 465 and 587. 465 is implicit TLS. 587 requires STARTTLS. `ignoreTLS` stays off. `rejectUnauthorized` stays true. TLS 1.2 is the minimum. There is no custom CA.

The probe letter subject and text are fixed in the mail module. A request cannot supply them. `POST /api/settings/mail/test` has an empty body. Saving settings does not send.

The password is AES-256-GCM ciphertext. An empty password field does not replace it. Do not log the password, the AUTH exchange, or a nodemailer error object. Operator text is one of the fixed phrases.

One send is in flight. The database connection is not held across that send. There is no second SIGTERM listener. A restart does not repeat a probe.

Do not add a digest, a schedule, or a second mail transport in this release.
